# The de Havilland Mosquito FB Mk VI, two Merlin 25s: a flight model written
# for glideslope from the aircraft's trials and Pilot's Notes, and held to them
# (assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml).
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name de Havilland Mosquito FB Mk VI
model mosquito-fb6
class second-world-war
start 220 0.45
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# An ESTIMATE: her Pilot's Notes give no tyre pressure. About 10,200 lb on
# each Dunlop main tyre over a contact patch of about 190 square inches, 45 to
# 60 psi; 50 taken. Dunlop pneumatic brakes, no anti-skid (the Maxaret came
# after the war).
brakes 50 none
